    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="1107" n="1005" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1005"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-21T18:00:00+00:00">January 21, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 21—3:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Embassy’s 13, January 12, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d867-f1"/> concerning Spanish proposal made in London that
                    British extraterritorial rights in Spanish Zone of Morocco be relinquished.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office now supplements its previous statement with the following
                    information: The British Ambassador at Madrid reports that he was assured that
                    the above Spanish proposal had no connection whatever with trade negotiations
                    now being conducted in Madrid, and that some time ago the Spanish Government
                    instructed the Spanish Embassy at London to take up the question of
                    extraterritorial rights with the Foreign Office but the instruction had been
                    overlooked by the Spanish Embassy until a few days ago.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office seemed entirely satisfied with the above explanation and no
                    longer holds the opinion mentioned in the last paragraph of the telegram under
                    reference.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office has merely acknowledged the Spanish Embassy’s note containing
                    the proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
